/**
 * Device gaps, November 2026 round, part two: biopsy and localisation systems, embolisation devices, palliative
 * drainage and stents, laboratory analysers, endoscopic ablation and cholangioscopy, and automated breast ultrasound.
 * Filled from docs/proposals/gap-census-2026-11.md (types biopsy-systems, embolisation-devices,
 * palliative-home-devices, and the analyser, localisation, cholangioscopy, Barrett ablation and automated breast
 * ultrasound rows of lab-instruments, haematopathology-tests, serum-tumour-markers, margin-intraop-devices,
 * breast-imaging-localisation, mri-ct-scanners, ablation-systems, endoscopy-capsule-sampling and imaging-examinations).
 *
 * Method as in src/data/devices-gaps-2026-11.ts: every FDA number was read from openFDA on 4 November 2026, indication
 * wording is quoted from the 510(k) summary PDF where one was readable, NICE wording from the guidance pages, and trial
 * figures from the abstracts as Europe PMC returns them, each DOI resolved there first.
 *
 * Embolic microspheres need a caution the regulator records make plain: several are cleared under product codes named
 * for uterine fibroids (NAJ) or prostate enlargement (NOY), and the 510(k) indications speak of "hypervascular tumors";
 * none of the American clearances read here covers loading a drug into the beads, which is a European labelling claim.
 */
